      "content": "Originalism argues that the Constitution should be interpreted according to the original understanding of its text when it was adopted. Proponents believe that the meaning of the text is fixed by the framers' intent or the public meaning at the time of ratification. This approach aims to limit the power of judges by preventing them from imposing their own personal policy preferences onto the law. Essentially, it keeps the Constitution stable and faithful to the will of the people in the nation's founding.",
